    "note": "Register the palace to three surviving Banqueting House corners on the Historic Royal Palaces plan, then transfer the Fisher engraving through the same hall. The traced fourth corner and the independently traced Holbein Gate center are within 0.28 m and 0.77 m, respectively, of their comparison controls. Placement uses the modern Whitehall datum and the surviving hall’s alignment. The surveyed plans locate the quay and courts. Contemporary Mapzen samples set the visual ground origin at 4.17 m. Two bounded, dated grades expose the court surfaces. The traced waterfront joins the mapped Thames through a bounded 2.21 m illustrative stage, with the lower steps reaching the water. Historical placement requires an explicit viewingDate within the recorded appearance interval; excluded from the default current world."
